# Rolls-Royce Silver Cloud II four-door saloon, 1959-1962.
#
# The Silver Cloud II replaced the six with the 6,230 cc aluminium V8. The body
# is unchanged from the Cloud I: same 5,384 mm length, 1,829 mm width, 1,600 mm
# height and 3,124 mm wheelbase, same radiator, same wings, same glazing. At
# sprite scale the two marks are indistinguishable, so this car is built from
# the Cloud I master rather than modelled again, and carries the Cloud II dates
# so that the 1959-1962 period is covered by a car of the right mark.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Silver_Cloud
#
# Colours: Black, Silver, Maroon and Grey were period Rolls-Royce finishes.
#
# Weight: 10 in total (black 5, silver 2, maroon 2, grey 1). The Cloud II is
# rarer than the Cloud I in the parc, so the total is lower.
#
# Speed 165 km/h; comfort 90/465 (line). Classes 3,4.
# Dates: 1959-1962 with a road tail to about 1985.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rolls-royce-silver-cloud-ii.blend, derived from
# citycars/4.5/rolls-royce-silver-cloud-i.blend. References:
# citycars/references/rolls-royce-silver-cloud-ii/ (gitignored). Images via
# Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=RollsRoyceSilverCloudII(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=5
